# Fast sanity check: same beam as mac_185MeV.mac but only 1000 protons.
# Run it directly (NOT through run_master.sh, which appends its own
# /run/beamOn):
#
#     build/exampleB1 mac_smoketest.mac MSC        # default: BERT
#     build/exampleB1 mac_smoketest.mac MSC BIC     # compare hadronic models
#     build/exampleB1 mac_smoketest.mac MSC BERT_HP
#
# Watch stdout for "==== HADRONIC INELASTIC MODEL: ... ====" printing back
# what you asked for -- if you passed an unrecognized value it falls back to
# BERT and prints a warning to say so.
#
# Deliberately does not set an output file name, so it tests only the thing
# that was broken: that /gps/... resolves and that the user actions are
# registered and scoring. Output therefore lands in the RunAction default,
# recoils_nt_PKAs.csv -- so runs with different hadronic models will
# overwrite each other's file here; that's fine for a resolves-or-not check,
# just don't compare PKA counts between two smoketest runs from this file.
/run/initialize
/run/printProgress 100
/gps/particle proton
/gps/pos/type Plane
/gps/pos/shape Square
/gps/pos/halfx 0.5 cm
/gps/pos/halfy 0.5 cm
/gps/pos/centre 0 0 -4 cm
/gps/direction 0 0 1
/gps/energy 185 MeV
/run/beamOn 1000
